                        "title": "Interpretation 1: From a history textbook, discussing the position of women and society in Weimar Germany.",
                        "content": "This interpretation emphasizes the profound social progress made during the Weimar era. It argues that new legal rights, political suffrage, and expanding job opportunities fundamentally altered the lives of German women. It showcases the emergence of a new generation of independent, visible women who rejected the conservative, domestic lifestyles of their mothers."
