                        "title": "Interpretation 1: From a history textbook, published in 2015.",
                        "content": "The primary driver behind the surge in Nazi support after 1929 was the personal, charismatic appeal of Adolf Hitler himself. Hitler was a dynamic, highly modern communicator who utilised innovative campaigning tactics, such as his 'Hitler over Germany' flights, to project himself as a strong, energetic leader. At a time of national crisis, he was able to tap into the anxieties of ordinary citizens, presenting himself as a messianic figure who alone could restore German pride and order."
