                        "content": "This perspective focuses on the systemic collapse of the Weimar political structure. It argues that the Great Depression paralyzed the moderate parties, who could not agree on policies, forcing the government to rely on Article 48 emergency decrees that bypassed the Reichstag. In this view, democracy was already dead, and the conservative elites had to hand power to Hitler because his party was the largest in the parliament."
